Thank you for the Rev B package. It is a real step forward: the ground plane, the switched sensor rails and the per-port I2C segments are the right calls, and some of it goes beyond what we asked.
The attached review (MS-CAR-REV-B-001) checks the package against the 59 items and the release gate. Rev B is not yet released for fabrication. Please read section 1 first, then sections 5 and 6: the 6-layer Gerbers short 5 V to ground at the ESP32 header, the 4-layer has the watchdog input unconnected, and the 5 V input needs the protection and copper described in section 6 before the modem board can be held inside its 4.75 to 5.25 V window.
Two decisions from our side: the 4-layer board goes forward and the 6-layer is withdrawn; the 5 V input at J18 is accepted on the six conditions in section 6.4.
For the next package, please start with the response sheet against the 59 items and R1 to R17 (section 12, row 1), and send it with the evidence listed there. A schematic-only review before you lay out the board is welcome and may save a loop. I am glad to go through any item on a call.

