Good question. There is no PCB testing software as such. The reviews are done with Claude, working from the files you send: KiCad 10 (ERC, DRC with schematic parity and refilled zones, the Gerber viewer), our own scripts that read the board file, netlist, Gerbers and drill files, the part datasheets, IPC-2221 and a DC budget model. Every number is reproduced by a second independent pass before a review goes out. The tool is never the evidence; the files and the datasheets are.

Rather than describe it, I have written up the whole procedure as the attached release check (MS-CAR-CHK-001). It is the same set of checks we run on your package, with the KiCad steps and what pass means for each, plus the response sheet that should come with every package and a one-page list to tick before you send. If you run it on the files before they leave you, the next review should be a confirmation rather than a new list, and we save a loop on both sides.

Section 4 is the part to work through; Appendix A has the KiCad settings to set once. Call me if any check is unclear and we will go through it together.
